WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.300
All right.

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.890
Now I have to talk about something.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.540
Anybody who saw our program last night

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.160
is gonna demand that I discuss this,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.890
because something happened

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.780
in the middle of our show last night,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.970
just after we came back from commercial.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.750
And I've been doing this show a long time,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.220
and in all the many years
I've been doing Late Night

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.460
something like this has
never happened before.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.420
It was real. We didn't think
of this or contrive it.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.850
This just happened.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.650
I think you can tell when
you see the look on my face

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.110
that something real and
strange is unfolding.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.630
Check out this clip from
our show last night.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.090
I wanna mention something,
fall TV shows are back

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.230
on the air now...
(siren wailing)

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.460
Swear to god. We've been
doing this show for...

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.230
14 years.
Over 14 years.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.080
I have never heard this sound before.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.180
But everyone stay calm. What
is that all about, Jeff?

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.437
I think it's probably a test.

00:00:53.437 --> 00:00:54.580
We'll just double-check and make sure.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.680
Do they know we're taping a (beep) show?

00:00:58.181 --> 00:01:00.341
(audience laughs)
I'm serious!

00:01:00.341 --> 00:01:02.149
What the hell's that?

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:03.899
Klingons approaching!

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.440
The hell's goin' on?

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.440
I'm serious, I've never...
(audience applauds)

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.120
[Fire Safety Director] May I
have your attention, please?

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.410
May I have your attention?

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.381
This is the fire safety director speaking.

00:01:17.381 --> 00:01:19.680
Please be advised we have
received an alarm condition

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.460
on the fifth floor.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.830
Building personnel are
conducting an investigation

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.058
at this time.
Is this a New York subway?

00:01:26.058 --> 00:01:28.090
(audience laughs)

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.460
We should just air this
thing the way it is

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.010
and let the people out there know

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.705
how crappy this show is run!

00:01:34.705 --> 00:01:37.014
This is what you do.
(audience cheers)

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:39.014
It's unbelievable to me.

00:01:42.475 --> 00:01:46.660
So we just aired the show as
it all happened last night

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.765
and all of us were stunned.

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:50.510
I was thinking, "How could this happen?"

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.740
This is supposed to be a
professional broadcast.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.860
But my biggest question is who's that guy

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.950
making the announcement?

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.560
And he came back later in the next segment

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.150
when I was talking to Paget
Brewster, the second guest,

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.490
he came back and made more announcements.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.740
Well, anyway, it turns
out everything was fine.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.150
It was a false alarm.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.300
But this morning I had this burning idea.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.540
I wanted to grab a camera
crew and investigate

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.920
and meet the guy that
made that announcement.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.200
So I went downstairs.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.900
Here's what happened, take a look.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:22.895
Hi. How are you?

00:02:22.895 --> 00:02:24.290
Hello, how are ya?
Good to see ya.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.557
You too. How's everything?

00:02:25.557 --> 00:02:27.060
Are you Bruce?
Yes I am.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.326
Bruce Britt.
Yes.

00:02:28.326 --> 00:02:30.100
And what is your title?
Fire safety director.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.320
You're the fire safety director.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.535
And this is your station right here?

00:02:32.535 --> 00:02:33.368
Yes it is.

00:02:33.368 --> 00:02:35.550
You made an announcement
yesterday around...

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.300
I'm gonna say around six
o'clock in the evening.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.510
Is that right?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.640
We were taping a show,
were you aware of that?

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.020
Yes, I was.
Yeah.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.550
And your announcement,
actually, interrupted our show

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.930
and was heard by probably
three million viewers.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.370
Can we recreate that
announcement right now?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.240
Can we hear it just as you said it?

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.110
Okay.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.500
May I have your attention please?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.870
May I have your attention?

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.970
This is your fire safety
director speaking.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.330
We have received an alarm
condition on the fifth floor.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.020
Building personnel are conducting

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.950
an investigation at this time.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.550
Please stand by for further instructions.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.170
It went out to three
million, let's bump that up.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.250
It went out to 15 million
viewers last night.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.901
I'm including Telemundo, where
it was heard differently.

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:20.901
Silencio, silencio, una
dangerouso predicamento,

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.940
I think is how it was on Telemundo.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.930
Your voice is very good, did you ever...

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.210
If I just came up with some announcements

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.870
would you do those?
Sure.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:32.580
Okay. I repeat, I repeat, there
are onions on the griddle.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.640
Onions on the griddle.
Put on your admiral's hat.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.080
There are onions on the griddle.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.410
There are onions on the griddle.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.330
There are onions on the griddle, I repeat,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.040
there are onions on the griddle.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.027
Put on your admiral's hat.

00:03:42.027 --> 00:03:43.820
There are onions on the griddle.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.020
There are onions on the griddle.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:47.130
That sounds pretty good. Now try this one.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.850
Talent alert, talent alert.
There's a talent overload.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.320
Conan O'Brien is in the
building. Talent overload.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.660
Try that.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.980
Talent alert, talent alert.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.630
There's a talent overload in the building.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.250
Conan O'Brien is in the building.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.880
Yes! I love that.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.700
Let's take a look at
this console over here.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.190
Where are the scripted announcements?

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.023
Right to the right of us.

00:04:07.023 --> 00:04:09.120
Can you tell me what
you think of my voice?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.378
If you think I'd be any good at this?

00:04:10.378 --> 00:04:11.890
All right, go ahead.
Lemme try it in my voice.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:12.830
Which one should I use?

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.880
Do the alarm condition. Right here.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.200
Right here?
Yeah.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.040
Okay, check this out.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.260
Hey there, may I have
your attention please.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.860
This is your fire safety director.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.050
We have an alarm condition
on the fifth floor.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.280
The building personnel are
conducting an investigation.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.889
Will the fire warden on the fifth floor

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:30.280
pick up the warden phone immediately

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.478
if you would?

00:04:31.478 --> 00:04:32.761
Maybe a little bit lower.

00:04:32.761 --> 00:04:34.340
Little bit lower?
Just a little bit lower.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.450
Yeah, that's not gonna work for me.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.819
I might even go higher.

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:38.110
All right, well, try that.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.200
May I have your attention please?

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.830
Your fire safety director,
we have an alarm condition

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.420
on the fifth floor.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.390
Building personnel are
conducting an investigation.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.630
Will the fire warden on the fifth floor

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.232
pick up the warden phone immediately?

00:04:49.232 --> 00:04:50.283
All right, that's all right.

00:04:50.283 --> 00:04:51.963
I think we can work with that.

00:04:51.963 --> 00:04:52.835
We can work with that.
Really?

00:04:52.835 --> 00:04:54.285
Yeah, I think we can work with that.

00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:55.260
That sounded horrible.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:58.010
Look at this one right here.
(laughing) It's for odors.

00:04:58.857 --> 00:05:01.770
"Speak slowly, calmly and clearly."

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.850
Can you read that one for us?

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.540
Okay. May I have your attention please?

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.120
This is your fire safety
director speaking.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.980
We are experiencing a smell,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.110
odor or smoke condition from
outside of our building.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:19.397
This is due to construction
work, repair work or other.

00:05:19.397 --> 00:05:21.720
"Or other!"
We are adjusting...

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.100
"Or other."

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.090
Kinda leaves it out there.
Right.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.360
The odor might be...

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.020
Could be a lotta things.
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.542
True.

00:05:32.542 --> 00:05:34.000
(alarm beeping)
Uh-oh! What's that?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.030
What happened? What's goin' on?

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:35.863
Uh-oh.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:37.773
What happened?

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.500
Somebody's working upstairs, that's all.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.750
It just lets me know that somebody's

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:43.910
working on one of the devices.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.340
My heart just stopped for a second.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.790
I'm so scared.
You're all right, I'm here.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.610
You're all right, you're good.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.850
You're gonna take care of me?

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.683
I got you.

00:05:51.614 --> 00:05:52.840
Everything's good.
I feel safe around you.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:53.760
Feel safe?
Yes.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.593
All right.

00:05:54.593 --> 00:05:56.910
Could I have a hug, please?
Aw, all right.

00:05:59.183 --> 00:06:00.410
You know what?

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.480
If it hadn't happened we never woulda met.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.450
That's true.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.420
I think it's nice that we met.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.253
So do I.

00:06:07.115 --> 00:06:08.806
(laughing) You didn't seem too convinced.

00:06:08.806 --> 00:06:11.660
No, that wasn't good. That was not good.

00:06:13.286 --> 00:06:15.810
Please welcome our building's
deputy fire safety director,

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.643
Bruce Britt!

00:06:17.715 --> 00:06:20.548
(audience cheers)

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.437
Good to see you, Bruce.
All right, how you doin'?

00:06:25.437 --> 00:06:28.260
I'm doin' good now! Ah, Bruce...

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:32.020
Bruce is gonna help take us
out to commercial tonight.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.755
Bruce, take it away.

00:06:33.755 --> 00:06:36.400
May I have your attention?
May I have your attention?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.870
Please, we'll be right
back with our first guest,

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:40.703
Jake Gyllenhall.

